 Trading Plan: Can Nifty 50 rebound towards 22,600, Bank Nifty move above 55,000?
 In case of a rebound, the Nifty 50 may face resistance in the 22,600-22,800 zone, while immediate support is placed at 22,200, followed by 22,000 as a crucial support level.
 Sunil Shankar Matkar
 October 05, 2026 / 07:33 IST 
 --> 
 Nifty Trading Plan for October 5, 2026 
 Nifty 50 may face resistance in 22,600-22,800 zone
 Immediate support is placed at 22,200, followed by 22,000 as crucial support
 Bank Nifty may attempt to move towards the 55,000-55,400 zone
 Did our AI summary help? 
 Market Mastery
After a severe correction in recent weeks and with the index entering oversold territory, the possibility of a near-term rebound cannot be ruled out, although the broader structure remains under the control of the bears. In case of a rebound, the Nifty 50 may face resistance in the 22,600-22,800 zone, while immediate support is placed at 22,200, followed by 22,000 as a crucial support level. Meanwhile, the Bank Nifty may attempt to move towards the 55,000-55,400 zone, which acted as a resistance zone in the previous week. On the downside, support is placed in the 54,000-53,700 zone, according to experts.
On October 1, the Nifty 50 plummeted 199 points, or 0.88 percent, to 22,422, while the Bank Nifty fell 182 points, or 0.33 percent, to 54,451. Market breadth was firmly in favour of the bears, with 2,556 stocks declining compared with 729 stocks advancing on the NSE.
 Jatin Gedia, Technical Research Analyst, VP, Derivatives & Technical Research at Teji Mandi 
Nifty witnessed a sharp recovery after testing the 22,220 - 22,180 support zone (April 2026 swing low) and closed above 22,400. After declining for eight consecutive weeks, Nifty tested the 200-week exponential moving average at 22,384. According to the Elliott wave principle, Nifty might have completed a 24-month wave four triangle consolidation and is now poised to resume its primary uptrend.
Looking at seasonality, Nifty has closed in the green on 7 out of the last 10 occasions during October. The Relative Strength Index's extreme oversold reading of 22.57 is likely to trigger a trend reversal or a short term bounce.
On the derivatives front, maximumPut open interest is placed at 22,000 followed by 21,500 while the maximum Call open interest is placed at 23,000 followed by 23,500. Open interest increased across 22,500 - 22,650 CE strikes implying immediate resistance. Sustaining above 22,600 - 22,650 could trigger a short covering move.
While Brent Crude above $100 a barrel and a rising US 10 year bond yields pose a near-term risk that could delay the recovery process, considering the extreme reading on the momentum indicator and the overall price structure we believe a reversal is around the corner.
 Strategy : Buy Nifty October Futures at around 22,531, with a stop-loss of 22,380 and target of 22,700, 22,890.
 Jay Mehta, Technical Research at JM Financial Services 
Nifty continued its negative trend and broke below the 23,000 zone during the last week, with selling pressure remaining elevated. The index declined to 22,217 before witnessing a mild recovery from the important 22,000–22,200 support zone. Nifty remains below its short-, medium- and long-term moving averages, keeping the broader trend bearish.
However, after sustained selling pressure during August and September, the index is in an oversold zone, raising the possibility of a short-term bounce. A sustained move above 22,600 for one hour could trigger some positive momentum, but the broader trend remains weak.
 Strategy : Sell on rise strategy can be used around key resistances at 22,750, 22,900 and 23,100. Fresh shorts in Nifty Futures can be considered below 22,200 for targets of 21,800 and 22,000.
 Jatin Gedia, Technical Research Analyst, VP, Derivatives & Technical Research at Teji Mandi 
Bank Nifty has been more resilient to the broader market decline as it continued to consolidate between 53,500 and 55,200. Last week, it tested the 53,700 - 53,500 zone and bounced back to close above the 54,000 level. It respected the lower end of the reverse channel at 54,000 indicating a pullback from the support zone is likely.
With key heavyweights HDFC Bank showing signs of holding crucial 61.8 percent Fibonacci support at Rs 708 and ICICI Bank holding the lower end of the reverse channel at Rs 1,290, a reversal of the current decline is set up. We expect Bank Nifty to rise towards 55,900 - 56,200 where resistance exists in the form of a gap area formed on September 24.
 Strategy : Buy Bank Nifty October Futures at around 54,800, with a stop-loss of 54,300 and target of 56,200.
 Jay Mehta, Technical Research at JM Financial Services 
Bank Nifty showed relatively better resilience than Nifty over the last three sessions, holding the 53,800 support zone and moving sideways. However, the broader setup remains bearish after the breakdown below 55,500. The index is trading below its short-, medium- and long-term moving averages, while momentum and trend indicators continue to indicate weakness.
A break below 53,800 could open the way towards 53,500 and 53,000. On the upside, 55,500–55,800 is likely to act as a strong resistance zone.

